DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The sswwaabb() function copies _n bytes from the array pointed to by _f_r_o_m to
       the  array  pointed  to  by _t_o, exchanging adjacent even and odd bytes.
       This function is used to exchange data between machines that have  dif‐
       ferent low/high byte ordering.

       This  function does nothing when _n is negative.  When _n is positive and
       odd, it handles _n_-_1 bytes as above, and does something unspecified with
       the last byte.  (In other words, _n should be even.)

